<article id="top" class="container doorway">
  <p class="eyebrow">Tour</p>
  <h1>The tour</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every page here shows the framework doing the thing. Pick the angle.</p>
  <ul class="doors">
    <li><a href="/tour/derived/">Derived</a><span>One model, and the seventeen things the schema produces, each pointing back at its lines.</span></li>
    <li><a href="/tour/seams/">The seams</a><span>A single POST /api/leads and the seventeen named handoffs it crosses.</span></li>
    <li><a href="/tour/walkthrough/">The walkthrough</a><span>One model becomes a database, an API and a UI, fifteen steps at a time.</span></li>
    <li><a href="/tour/ripple/">The ripple</a><span>Change one line of the schema and watch what moves, and what does not.</span></li>
    <li><a href="/tour/loop/">The loop</a><span>Scaffold, run, migrate, deploy, watch, extend: the developer loop as one surface.</span></li>
    <li><a href="/tour/field/">One field</a><span>One field, all the way down.</span></li>
  </ul>
</article>

